    "result": "I implemented `RateLimiter` in `solution.py` and wrote 25 tests in `tests/test_solution.py`. All 25 pass with `python -m pytest -q tests`. I did not run the coverage, CRAP, mutation or bandit gates, so I can't say whether they pass.\n\n- **Implementation:** Each client has a list of `(time, cost)` records. Expired records are dropped on each call. `retry_after` counts how long until enough old records expire for the cost to fit.\n- **Validation order:** Cost is checked before time, so a call with an invalid cost doesn't move the limiter's clock forward. The spec doesn't say which comes first.\n- **Tests:** They cover argument validation, the exact window boundary, rejected requests not using budget, client isolation, costs above 1, `retry_after`, and time going backwards.\n- **Test fix:** One test of mine had a wrong expected value, which I corrected.",
